---
# Nothing here is for the user to fill in. The administrator's installer (ood/install.sh) writes the cluster id, the partition and the
# hours into this file, and the install folder and proxy path into the session script, once.
title: "Bhaskera"
description: |
  Bhaskera's home page: create a recipe, train, chat, benchmark and register models. It runs as a small job under your own account
  (account, folders and limits are found for you) and only you can open it. Press **Launch**, then **Open Bhaskera**.
cluster: "__CLUSTER__"
form:
  - bc_queue
  - bc_num_hours
attributes:
  bc_queue:
    widget: hidden_field
    value: "__PARTITION__"
  bc_num_hours:
    widget: hidden_field
    value: __HOURS__
